rves self-centering. PIN-1 MARKER: a filled 0.40 mm dot on F.SilkS and F.Fab beside pad 1 (top-left), centred at (-2.5, -1.3), 0.25 mm clear of the pad edge. The pre-existing filled triangle at the BOTTOM-RIGHT (beside pad 3) is DELIBERATELY RETAINED - do not delete it: LCSC/EasyEDA's own reference footprint places its triangle at the same corner, so it marks a real feature of the package, not pin 1. The two marks say different things: triangle = package corner, dot = pin 1. The triangle alone was ambiguous enough that the assembler repeatedly asked which pin is 1, which is why the dot was added rather than the triangle moved. Y IS UNCHANGED (0.8 tall, +/-1.0), so the 0.710 mm clearance to the Kailh socket pad above each LED is untouched; the courtyard grew in x only, +/-1.5 -> +/-2.25 - it bounds the BODY AND PADS (outer edge +/-2.05) plus a 0.20 mm margin, NOT the silkscreen. The pin-1 dot deliberately sits outside it, which is normal: a courtyard is a placement/collision envelope for the physical part, and sizing it to enclose a silk marker made it 0.80 mm too wide on each side. Pin numbering unchanged: 1 VDD, 2 DOUT, 3 VSS, 4 DIN.")
