	(footprint "poly_kb:BY25Q64ES-LGA8-2x3"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "5384a54e-1727-491a-a408-6567a8547a26")
		(at 195.2244 46.4312 90)
		(descr "BOYAMICRO BY25Q64ESCIG(R) / LCSC C50176394. 8-pad LGA8 2x3 mm serial flash. Land pattern derived from datasheet Rev 2.6 section 9.5 nominals: D 2.00, E 3.00, pitch e 0.50 BSC, span Nd 1.50 BSC, pad b 0.25 x L 0.45. Signal lands are b wide by L+0.15 mm, the 0.15 mm being an outward toe extension - LGA has no side-wettable flank, so without it there is no inspectable fillet. Pin order follows the section 9.5 Top View: 4,3,2,1 left-to-right along the top edge, 5,6,7,8 left-to-right along the bottom, which is rotated 90 degrees relative to the superseded DFN_XGIQ TR_WIN footprint. Pad 9 is the exposed pad, which datasheet Note 1 states is FLOATING inside the package. The land is 1.60 x 0.20, matching the section 9.5 nominals D1 (width) and E1 (height) - the exposed metal is a thin horizontal strip, not a large rectangle; h 0.15 brackets the same height on the opposite side of the drawing. It clears the signal lands by 0.95 mm. Tying it to GND is harmless since there is no internal connection.")
		(tags "flash SPI LGA8 2x3 BOYAMICRO BY25Q64")
